"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkmy_blog=globalThis.webpackChunkmy_blog||[]).push([[2151],{2270(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"review-FCAJ-5","metadata":{"permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-5","source":"@site/aws/FCAJ5.md","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-04 Cost optimization on AWS\\"","description":"Hello everyone, welcome back to Nghia\'s Blog! In our journey into Cloud and DevOps, we\'re often overwhelmed by flashy technologies like AI, Kubernetes, and Serverless. But there\'s an extremely practical skill, not at all glamorous, that determines the survival of a project: Cost Optimization.","date":"2026-03-24T15:32:00.724Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"AWS","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/aws"},{"inline":true,"label":"FCAJ","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/fcaj"},{"inline":true,"label":"blog","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/blog"}],"readingTime":2.47,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Pham Trong Nghia","title":"Administrator","url":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811","imageURL":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811.png","key":"admin","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"review-FCAJ-5","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-04 Cost optimization on AWS\\"","authors":["admin"],"tags":["AWS","FCAJ","blog"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-03 Gen AI on AWS - Kiro\\"","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-4"}},"content":"Hello everyone, welcome back to **Nghia\'s Blog**! In our journey into Cloud and DevOps, we\'re often overwhelmed by flashy technologies like AI, Kubernetes, and Serverless. But there\'s an extremely practical skill, not at all glamorous, that determines the survival of a project: **Cost Optimization**.\\r\\n\\r\\nToday, I\'ll be reviewing some incredibly valuable (literally) knowledge from the next lesson of our First Cloud AI Journey!\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. The Importance of Cost Optimization:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Cost optimization is one of the two core values \u200b\u200bthat engineers bring to a business (besides helping the business make money). While not a particularly \\"new or glamorous\\" technology topic, it is vital and always a top priority.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. Cost Optimization Methods on AWS:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Choosing the Right Resources**: Avoid bringing your entire physical server configuration (on-premise) to the cloud. On the cloud, allocate just enough configuration for current needs and scale as needed. Pay attention to the pricing of each service (e.g., storage capacity, read/write IOPS).\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Payment Methods**:\\r\\n  - _Reserved Instances / Savings Plans_: Commit to long-term use (1 year or 3 years) to receive high discounts.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - _Spot Instances_: Rent surplus AWS resources at extremely low prices, but AWS can reclaim them at any time (suitable for applications that are prone to interruptions).\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Automatic Resource On/Off**: For test or internal environments, only turn on servers during working hours (8 hours/day) and automatically turn them off at the end of the day to save costs.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Use Serverless or Fully Managed services**: Pay based on the number of requests or actual usage instead of paying for a server running 24/7. Suitable for applications with inconsistent traffic.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Optimized architecture design**: Refer to AWS Reference Architectures to balance technical requirements and costs.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Cost management (AWS Budgets & Tags)**:\\r\\n  - Use Tags to clearly allocate costs to each department and project.\\r\\n  - Set Budgets to limit budgets and receive early alerts before exceeding the allowed amount.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. Tools and Support:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Using AI (AWS Kiro CLI)**: Kiro can be used to automatically generate best practice checklists to optimize costs instead of doing it manually.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **AWS Pricing Calculator**: An important tool for estimating costs before actually building the system. Note that prices will vary depending on the region. For example, Malaysia or Thailand may be 10-20% cheaper than Singapore.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **AWS Support Packages**: Understand the four support packages (Basic, Developer, Business, Enterprise). For a real-world production environment, it is recommended to use at least the Business package, or Enterprise (with dedicated support engineers) for large systems.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 4. Practice and Self-Study:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Set up a secure AWS account (enable MFA for the Root user, create an IAM user).\\r\\n\\r\\n- Install AWS Budgets to manage your personal budget and avoid unexpected expenses.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Install and use **AWS Kiro IDE & CLI**.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Additional** research: It is mandatory to independently read and learn about the **AWS Well-Architected Framework** to understand the core principles of designing standard cloud systems.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n##\\r\\n\\r\\nWatch the video below to learn about FCAJ:\\r\\n\\r\\n- \ud83d\udd17 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UIw8UxGZCHA&list=PLahN4TLWtox3TSYFbN1DNX7NZgTVXNj3x&index=5\\r\\n\\r\\n---"},{"id":"review-FCAJ-4","metadata":{"permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-4","source":"@site/aws/FCAJ4.md","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-03 Gen AI on AWS - Kiro\\"","description":"Hello everyone, welcome back to Nghia\'s Blog! If our previous articles discussed cloud infrastructure, today we\'ll move on to a completely new and incredibly exciting chapter: The Intervention of AI in Software Development.","date":"2026-03-24T15:19:24.607Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"AWS","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/aws"},{"inline":true,"label":"FCAJ","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/fcaj"},{"inline":true,"label":"blog","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/blog"}],"readingTime":2.95,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Pham Trong Nghia","title":"Administrator","url":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811","imageURL":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811.png","key":"admin","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"review-FCAJ-4","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-03 Gen AI on AWS - Kiro\\"","authors":["admin"],"tags":["AWS","FCAJ","blog"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-04 Cost optimization on AWS\\"","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-5"},"nextItem":{"title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-02 Management Console\\"","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-3"}},"content":"Hello everyone, welcome back to **Nghia\'s Blog**! If our previous articles discussed cloud infrastructure, today we\'ll move on to a completely new and incredibly exciting chapter: **The Intervention of AI in Software Development**.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn particular, if you\'ve ever wondered about the difference between a regular AI (like ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude) and an AI Agent, this summary of First Cloud AI Journey\'s latest video will answer all your questions!\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. The Evolution of AI in Software Development (SDLC):\\r\\n\\r\\n- **2024**: AI acts as an assistant, helping developers write code faster.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **2025**: AI agents emerge capable of handling complex tasks and executing them end-to-end, with humans only playing a review role.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Future**: Towards Autonomous Agents \u2013 fully automated agents that can work independently and collaboratively without human intervention.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. Spec-Driven Development:\\r\\n\\r\\n- When working on complex projects, simply chatting (vibe coding) with AI is insufficient and easily leads to failure.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Instead, Spec-Driven Development should be applied: Provide detailed descriptions and requirements of the logic, business logic, and system before starting to code. AI (like AWS Kiro) will rely on these specification documents to build a more accurate product.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. Key Features of AWS Kiro IDE:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Supports two coding methodologies**: Vibe coding (free-flowing chat using natural language) and Spec-driven coding (guiding users to create detailed requirements documents before coding).\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Kiro IDE Agent Hook**: Allows setting up automated actions based on events. For example, every time a file is saved, the Agent will automatically generate/update the _changelog.md_ file or run unit tests, optimizing the code.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Context Management & Steering Files**: Connects Kiro with project documents so the AI \u200b\u200bunderstands the context. Kiro can be requested to automatically generate steering files (such as _product.md, structure.md_) from an existing project. Supports creating user interfaces from uploaded image files.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Checkpoint Rollback**: Saves checkpoints for easy rollback if a test idea fails or if you want to change development direction.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Property-Based Testing (PBT)**: Automatically generates and runs tests to verify whether the AI \u200b\u200bcode you\'ve just written meets the business requirements specified in the Spec file.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 4. Kiro CLI (Kiro Command Line Interface):\\r\\n\\r\\n- Brings the power of AI Agents directly into the Terminal (supports Linux and macOS).\\r\\n\\r\\n- You can use natural language to build products and analyze bugs without opening the IDE.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Custom Agent: Allows you to create custom AI Agents for specific workflows (e.g., Agents for DevOps, Databases, or Code Review). Each Agent will be assigned permissions and provided with its own suitable toolset (MCP Server).\\r\\n\\r\\n## 5. Kiro Power:\\r\\n\\r\\n- To prevent AI from being \\"overloaded\\" by context (loading too many tools at once, causing slowdowns, excessive token consumption, and hallucinations), Kiro Power acts as \\"extended skill bundles.\\"\\r\\n\\r\\n- Dynamic Loading Mechanism: AI only loads and uses the right tools/contexts when truly necessary (like giving Doraemon a \\"talent cassette tape\\"). There is a Kiro Power ecosystem contributed by AWS, partners, and the community.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 6. Kiro Autonomous Agent & Enterprise Governance:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Autonomous Agent**: Capable of independently thinking of ways to do and execute tasks. Importantly, it can remember user feedback to avoid repeating past errors.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Team Governance**: Provides a dashboard for managing permissions and monitoring Kiro usage across the entire enterprise team.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 7. Costs and Study Recommendations:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Kiro offers paid packages based on credits (e.g., $20 for 1000 credits).\\r\\n  Within the First Cloud AI Journey program, students are encouraged to use a\\r\\n\\r\\n- Free Tier account (receiving 50 free credits per month) to support their studies and graduation project.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n##\\r\\n\\r\\nWatch the video below to learn about FCAJ:\\r\\n\\r\\n- \ud83d\udd17 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uAQCm4sm_1c&list=PLahN4TLWtox3TSYFbN1DNX7NZgTVXNj3x&index=4\\r\\n\\r\\n---"},{"id":"review-FCAJ-3","metadata":{"permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-3","source":"@site/aws/FCAJ3.md","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-02 Management Console\\"","description":"Hello everyone, welcome back to Nghia\'s Blog! Having grasped the fundamental concepts of Cloud Computing and AWS infrastructure in the previous lesson, today we\'ll begin to get hands-on with the actual system. How do we log in? What types of accounts are there? And most importantly for us developers: how do we control AWS with code instead of clicking the mouse?","date":"2026-03-24T15:08:35.089Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"AWS","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/aws"},{"inline":true,"label":"FCAJ","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/fcaj"},{"inline":true,"label":"blog","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/blog"}],"readingTime":2.07,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Pham Trong Nghia","title":"Administrator","url":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811","imageURL":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811.png","key":"admin","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"review-FCAJ-3","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-02 Management Console\\"","authors":["admin"],"tags":["AWS","FCAJ","blog"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-03 Gen AI on AWS - Kiro\\"","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-4"},"nextItem":{"title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-01 - Introduction to AWS\\"","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-2"}},"content":"Hello everyone, welcome back to **Nghia\'s Blog**! Having grasped the fundamental concepts of Cloud Computing and AWS infrastructure in the previous lesson, today we\'ll begin to get hands-on with the actual system. How do we log in? What types of accounts are there? And most importantly for us developers: how do we control AWS with code instead of clicking the mouse?\\r\\n\\r\\nLet\'s review the core concepts from the next video of our First Cloud AI Journey!\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. AWS Management Console and User Types:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Root User**: This is the original account created with email and password when you first register for AWS. It is recommended not to use this account for daily operations. Instead, enable two-factor authentication (MFA), keep it safe, and minimize its use.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **IAM User**: These are sub-accounts created from the Root User. This is the official account used to log in and interact with AWS services in practice. An Account ID (a 12-digit string) is required to log in to the IAM User.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. AWS Management Console Interface:\\r\\n\\r\\n- This is an intuitive graphical web interface (GUI). On the home page, you can search and access over 200 AWS services through the search bar or categories.\\r\\n\\r\\n- This interface is very suitable for beginners as it helps you easily visualize the components and easily create resources.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Provide a support center where users can submit requests for assistance in case of technical issues or payment-related problems (e.g., accidentally creating a resource and forgetting to close it, resulting in charges).\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. Other methods of interacting with AWS:\\r\\n\\r\\nBesides clicking on the Management Console interface, AWS provides two other methods for automation and programming:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **AWS CLI (Command Line Interface)**: Interact with AWS through command lines. Very useful for writing scripts to automate repetitive tasks. Instead of using email/password, the CLI uses an _Access Key_ and _Secret Access Key_ for authentication. It is extremely important to note: these keys must be kept absolutely secure and should not be uploaded to public platforms like GitHub to avoid breaches.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **AWS SDK (Software Development Kit)**: A software development kit that allows you to interact with AWS directly from the application\'s source code. Each programming language (such as Python, C++, Java, Node.js...) will have its own corresponding SDK. The SDK helps your application automatically call AWS APIs (for example, writing Python code to automatically create a virtual server).\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n##\\r\\n\\r\\nWatch the video below to learn about FCAJ:\\r\\n\\r\\n- \ud83d\udd17 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=95quNuhvMT0&list=PLahN4TLWtox3TSYFbN1DNX7NZgTVXNj3x&index=3\\r\\n\\r\\n---"},{"id":"review-FCAJ-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-2","source":"@site/aws/FCAJ2.md","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-01 - Introduction to AWS\\"","description":"Hello everyone, welcome back to Nghia\'s Blog! Continuing the series of articles on the First Cloud AI Journey (FCAJ) by AWS Study Group, in this article I will delve deeper into the foundational knowledge.","date":"2026-03-24T14:54:11.889Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"AWS","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/aws"},{"inline":true,"label":"FCAJ","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/fcaj"},{"inline":true,"label":"blog","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/blog"}],"readingTime":2.27,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Pham Trong Nghia","title":"Administrator","url":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811","imageURL":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811.png","key":"admin","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"review-FCAJ-2","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-01 - Introduction to AWS\\"","authors":["admin"],"tags":["AWS","FCAJ","blog"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-02 Management Console\\"","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-3"},"nextItem":{"title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Know before you join First Cloud AI Journey\\"","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-1"}},"content":"Hello everyone, welcome back to **Nghia\'s Blog**! Continuing the series of articles on the First Cloud AI Journey (FCAJ) by AWS Study Group, in this article I will delve deeper into the foundational knowledge.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf you are aiming for UI DevOps and similar systems, then understanding the nature of Cloud Computing and how to build a global AWS platform is essential. Below is what I learned from the second video of the course.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. New features of this year\'s First Cloud AI Journey program:\\r\\n\\r\\n- This year\'s course has been upgraded to keep up with technology trends by integrating GenAI.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Students will become familiar with and use the AWS Q virtual assistant (Amazon Q) throughout the program. This tool will support everything from summarizing knowledge, learning, applying it to work, to completing graduation projects.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. What is Cloud Computing?:\\r\\n\\r\\n- According to AWS\'s definition, cloud computing is the provision of IT services over the Internet using a \\"pay-as-you-go\\" model.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Unlike the traditional method (which requires purchasing hardware and building expensive and high-risk data centers), Cloud Computing is like renting resources (like renting a hotel room instead of buying a house outright).\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. Benefits of Cloud Computing:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Cost optimization**: Pay only for the amount of resources used.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Speed**: Enables faster product and application deployment thanks to readily available automation, AI, and security tools.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Service diversity**: AWS now offers tens of thousands of different services/features, instead of just renting virtual servers (EC2) or storage space as in its early days.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Global scalability**: Easily serves customers in other countries without needing to build physical infrastructure there.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 4. The concept of AWS global infrastructure:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Data Center**: A place containing tens of thousands of servers with customized components (from CPUs and GPUs to networks) specifically for AWS.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Availability Zone - AZ**: Consists of one or more data centers. AZs are located far apart to ensure that if one AZ fails (power outage, natural disaster), it will not affect other AZs. In practice, it is recommended to deploy applications across at least two AZs for safety.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Region**: A region contains at least three AZs. Regions operate independently. Currently, Southeast Asia has regions such as Singapore, Malaysia, and Thailand.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Edge Location and POP (Point of Presence)**: These are edge data centers that provide services such as CloudFront (CDN). AWS now has Edge Locations in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City, enabling significantly faster loading of static files (images, videos) for users in Vietnam.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Local Zone**: Like a miniature AZ, located locally (for example, in Vietnam and directly connected to the Singapore Region) to minimize latency and meet local data security standards.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n##\\r\\n\\r\\nWatch the video below to learn about FCAJ:\\r\\n\\r\\n- \ud83d\udd17 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qVCF7UjYC5s&list=PLahN4TLWtox3TSYFbN1DNX7NZgTVXNj3x&index=2\\r\\n\\r\\n---"},{"id":"review-FCAJ-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-1","source":"@site/aws/FCAJ1.md","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Know before you join First Cloud AI Journey\\"","description":"Hi everyone, welcome back to Nghia\'s Blog! If you\'re pursuing a career in Computer Science, especially if you\'re interested in Cloud Computing and DevOps, then you definitely can\'t miss the AWS ecosystem. Recently, I participated in the AWS Study Group\'s First Cloud AI Journey (FCAJ) program. This program is like a \\"roadmap\\" for newcomers to the world of cloud computing. Below is what I learned about the program from the first FCAJ video.","date":"2026-03-24T07:11:00.388Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"AWS","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/aws"},{"inline":true,"label":"FCAJ","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/fcaj"},{"inline":true,"label":"blog","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/tags/blog"}],"readingTime":2.35,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Pham Trong Nghia","title":"Administrator","url":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811","imageURL":"https://github.com/trongnghia1811.png","key":"admin","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"review-FCAJ-1","title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Know before you join First Cloud AI Journey\\"","authors":["admin"],"tags":["AWS","FCAJ","blog"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Review First Cloud AI Journey \\"Module 01-01 - Introduction to AWS\\"","permalink":"/my-docusaurus/aws/review-FCAJ-2"}},"content":"Hi everyone, welcome back to **Nghia\'s Blog**! If you\'re pursuing a career in Computer Science, especially if you\'re interested in Cloud Computing and DevOps, then you definitely can\'t miss the AWS ecosystem. Recently, I participated in the AWS Study Group\'s First Cloud AI Journey (FCAJ) program. This program is like a \\"roadmap\\" for newcomers to the world of cloud computing. Below is what I learned about the program from the first FCAJ video.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. What is First Cloud AI Journey (FCAJ)?\\r\\n\\r\\n- This is a community of people learning and working with AWS, where members support each other and share knowledge in a non-toxic environment.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Vision: Not just for certification exams, but for long-term career support, helping members become future tech leaders and inspire the next generation.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. Six core principles of the program:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Builder and Troubleshooter Spirit**: Ability to independently build products to solve real-world problems and independently troubleshoot when systems encounter issues.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Teamwork**: An extremely important skill in an era of constantly changing technology; the program encourages group registration and learning.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Resilience**: Perseverance and mutual support to meet the ever-increasing expectations of businesses, especially with the advent of AI.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Hands-on and Knowledge Sharing**: Qualifications must go hand in hand with practical skills. Skills are proven through practice and confidently sharing knowledge with the community.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Investing in Yourself**: Don\'t hesitate to invest time and money in learning and practicing.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Lifelong Learning**: A continuous learning journey (the program sets a 6-month target to motivate participants, but each person may have their own pace).\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. Practice and Projects:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Practical exercises are designed for students to start from scratch, rather than simply following pre-written instructions, fostering a deep understanding of how to apply the knowledge in practice.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Graduation requirement: Complete 5 projects.\\r\\n\\r\\n- The projects don\'t need to be massive; what matters is their accuracy, solving a business problem, and that you feel proud enough to include them on your CV or LinkedIn profile.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 4. Benefits of participation:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Participate in events and meetups organized by FCAJ in collaboration with universities, AWS partners, and IT companies (in Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City, and Da Nang).\\r\\n\\r\\n- Opportunities to present and share knowledge, thereby building your personal brand and potentially using it as a profile for the AWS Community Builder position.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Receive support from a community of over 50,000 members (primarily through WhatsApp).\\r\\n\\r\\n## 5. What do I need to prepare before starting? (Checklist):\\r\\n\\r\\n- A personal AWS account.\\r\\n\\r\\n- AWS Builder Profile account (to access more in-depth practice exercises).\\r\\n\\r\\n- WhatsApp account for communication and support.\\r\\n\\r\\n- A professional LinkedIn profile to update your learning progress and completed projects.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Join community channels: AWS Study Group Facebook/LinkedIn group, WordPress blog, and two YouTube channels (one theoretical, one practical).\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n##\\r\\n\\r\\nWatch the video below to learn about FCAJ:\\r\\n\\r\\n- \ud83d\udd17 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gz56QzLQ_Yo&list=PLahN4TLWtox3TSYFbN1DNX7NZgTVXNj3x\\r\\n\\r\\n---"}]}}')}}]);